  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nThursday night through Wednesday\nAssessment...low (20-30%) confidence on late week rain chances\n\nThe model consensus continues to point to late Thursday night into \nFriday evening for another, albeit low, chance of rain with the \npassage of another front. Given what has happened with the previous \nfront, I would not be surprised if the 20-40% chances for rain are \ndelayed until the Friday/Friday night time period.\n\nAs mentioned yesterday, northwest flow aloft means that any \ndisturbance moving through will be moisture starved. Thus the \nprospects for any rain outside of the more likely Friday/Friday \nnight time period is very limited.",
